    [CI]Fix the 406 error returned by the API when the PR content is too large. (#18481)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    The API refuses to render diffs exceeding its limits (20k total lines /
    1 MB raw data / 300 files) with HTTP 406.That is deterministic, so
    retrying cannot help; fall back to the github.com stream endpoint, which
    is not rate-limited by diff size.
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    NO
    ### How was this patch tested?
    This patch was tested locally by simulating the following scenarios:
    Normal PR content: A PR with a moderate amount of content. Verified that
    the API returns a normal response without any 406 error.
    Oversized PR content: A PR with a large amount of content (e.g., a large
    diff or many changed files). Verified that the API no longer returns a
    406 (Not Acceptable) error after the fix, and the request completes
    successfully.
    
    Both scenarios were tested locally, and the results matched
    expectations.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/8cc9aa5ad350f6f80cf3bebb298d410803ff75a9
    
